    "body": "On AMD ROCm platforms like MI300A in APU mode, `is_cuda_alike()` returns `True` but the vLLM C extension may not have the GPU ops registered (e.g. when built without ROCm support), causing an `AttributeError` at model load time in `GeluAndMul`, `NewGELU`, `FastGELU`, and `QuickGELU`. This PR adds `hasattr` guards so these activations fall back to their pure-Python `forward_native` implementations when the `_C` ops are missing. A regression test is included that simulates this exact scenario by mocking `is_cuda_alike=True` with an empty `torch.ops._C` namespace.",
    "changed_files": 2,
