  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile this correctly handles the `AttributeError` by falling back to `forward_native`, it's worth noting that other activation layers in this file (like `SiluAndMul`, `MulAndSilu`, and `FatreluAndMul`) still directly access `torch.ops._C` without guards. On platforms where the C extension is missing or incomplete, these will still trigger the same `AttributeError`. Consider applying this pattern consistently across all activation layers that rely on custom `_C` ops to ensure robust fallback behavior throughout the module.",
      "created_at": "2026-04-13T19:11:19Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -271,10 +271,11 @@ def __init__(self, approximate: str = \"none\"):\n             or current_platform.is_cpu()\n             or current_platform.is_xpu()\n         ):\n-            if approximate == \"none\":\n-                self.op = torch.ops._C.gelu_and_mul\n-            elif approximate == \"tanh\":\n-                self.op = torch.ops._C.gelu_tanh_and_mul\n+            op_name = \"gelu_and_mul\" if approximate == \"none\" else \"gelu_tanh_and_mul\"\n+            if hasattr(torch.ops._C, op_name):\n+                self.op = getattr(torch.ops._C, op_name)\n+            else:\n+                self._forward_method = self.forward_native",
